    <!-- ============ GUARD GAP ============

         The service that closes apps can be turned off, and Android will not let
         an app prevent that. So the price is charged inside ALIVE instead: the
         day is marked, the mark is visible until a quest pays for it, and the
         copy never claims to know who flipped the switch. -->
    <string name="guard_off_heading">ALIVE isn\'t watching</string>
    <string name="guard_off_body">The service that closes apps is off, so nothing is being closed right now.</string>
    <string name="guard_repair_needed">Turn it back on and finish one quest. Until then today is not a kept day.</string>
    <string name="guard_back_heading">The guard is back on</string>
    <string name="guard_back_body">Nothing is being missed any more. Today still shows as unguarded, because that stretch happened.</string>
    <string name="guard_repair_done">The mark stays on today. The streak is intact.</string>
    <string name="guard_who_turned_it_off">ALIVE can\'t tell whether you turned it off or the phone did to save battery.</string>
    <string name="guard_enable_action">Turn the guard back on</string>
    <string name="guard_profile_line">Today had a stretch with the guard off.</string>
    <string name="cd_guard_mark">Pixel figure, awake and looking sideways.</string>
    <string name="permissions_accessibility_why">Accessibility is how ALIVE closes an app when its time is up. Without it nothing is closed, and the day is marked as unguarded.</string>

